{title: Come Thou Long-Expected Jesus}
{key: C}
{time: 3/4}

{start_of_verse: 1}
[C]Come Thou [Am]long ex[F]pected [G]Jesus
[C]Born to [Am]set Thy [Dm]people [C]free
[C]From our [Am]fears and [F]sins re[G]lease us
[C]Let us [Am]find our [Dm]rest in [C]Thee
[Em]Israel's [Am]strength and [Dm]conso[G]lation
[C]Hope of [Am]all the [Dm]earth Thou [G]art
[C]Dear de[F]sire of [C]every [G]nation
[C]Joy of [F]every [G]longing [C]heart.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 2}
[C]Born Thy [Am]people [F]to de[G]liver
[C]Born a [Am]child and [Dm]yet a [C]King
[C]Born to [Am]reign in [F]us fo[G]rever
[C]Now Thy [Am]gracious [Dm]kingdom [C]bring
[Em]By Thine [Am]own e[Dm]ternal [G]Spirit
[C]Rule in [Am]all our [Dm]hearts a[G]lone
[C]By Thine [F]all suf[C]ficient [G]merit
[C]Raise us [F]to Thy [G]glorious [C]throne.
{end_of_verse}
